{"assets":["/statement-assets/89665619b58c9a479c67c974eec22291f6a1d1bfa740d19cd7ba49add3b4bb1b.png","/statement-assets/0a3bf735134ef272dcc90502026819bf7fbd3ce8a5a04c566628f1447379fddf.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"601","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. The Two Routes"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In Absurdistan, there are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" towns (numbered "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" through "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":") and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" bidirectional railways. There is also an absurdly simple road network — for each pair of different towns "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"kind":"text","text":", there is a bidirectional road between towns "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"if and only if"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" there is no railway between them. Travelling to a different town using one railway or one road always takes exactly one hour."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A train and a bus leave town "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" at the same time. They both have the same destination, town "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", and don't make any stops on the way (but they can wait in town "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The train can move only along railways and the bus can move only along roads."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You've been asked to plan out routes for the vehicles; each route can use any road/railway multiple times. One of the most important aspects to consider is safety — in order to avoid accidents at railway crossings, the train and the bus must not arrive at the same town (except town "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":") simultaneously."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Under these constraints, what is the minimum number of hours needed for both vehicles to reach town "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" (the maximum of arrival times of the bus and the train)? Note, that bus and train are not required to arrive to the town "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" at the same moment of time, but are allowed to do so."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ n ≤ 400"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0 ≤ m ≤ n(n - 1) / 2"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of towns and the number of railways respectively."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":", denoting a railway between towns "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"v"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ u, v ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u ≠ v"},{"kind":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You may assume that there is at most one railway connecting any two towns."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output one integer — the smallest possible time of the later vehicle's arrival in town "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":". If it's impossible for at least one of the vehicles to reach town "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", output "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":" - 1"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 2\n1 3\n3 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"2\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"4 6\n1 2\n1 3\n1 4\n2 3\n2 4\n3 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 5\n4 2\n3 5\n4 5\n5 1\n1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first sample, the train can take the route "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/89665619b58c9a479c67c974eec22291f6a1d1bfa740d19cd7ba49add3b4bb1b.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":" and the bus can take the route "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/0a3bf735134ef272dcc90502026819bf7fbd3ce8a5a04c566628f1447379fddf.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":". Note that they can arrive at town "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":" at the same time."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second sample, Absurdistan is ruled by railwaymen. There are no roads, so there's no way for the bus to reach town "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"4"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"601A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/601/problem/A"}